From a50a9bba06ed5e11abc2e446bba41e7bdc68e3a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zac <zac@zacbowling.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Jan 2026 19:18:35 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] mt76: mt7925/mt7921: Add mutex protection for
 ieee80211_iterate callbacks

This patch series adds proper mutex protection to prevent NULL pointer
dereferences and race conditions in the MediaTek mt7925 and mt7921 WiFi
drivers.

Key fixes:
- Add mutex protection around ieee80211_iterate_active_interfaces() calls
- Add NULL checks before dereferencing link state pointers
- Handle key removal gracefully during MLO roaming
- Protect runtime PM and reset work functions
- Move mutex from iterator callbacks to calling functions for correctness

These fixes prevent kernel crashes during WiFi state transitions,
particularly during suspend/resume, channel switches, and MLO roaming.

Tested on Framework Laptop 16 with MT7925 WiFi adapter.

Signed-off-by: Zac Bowling <zac@zacbowling.com>
